(472060, 44929, 9146, '<td valign="top">nice pic<br/> <br/>try this, <br/> <br/>next time when you convert to grayscale using the gradient knock out or down the blue channel first before you lay the grant layer on. I''m not sure how you do this in PS but in elements 2 you go to adjust color-collor variations- make sure it''s set on midtones and then desturate...(I think ) blue You''ll get a Yellowish cast. apply your gradient layer. you''ll be surprised at the results</td>', 'nice pic try this,  next time when you convert to grayscale using the gradient knock out or down the blue channel first before you lay the grant layer on. I''m not sure how you do this in PS but in elements 2 you go to adjust color-collor variations- make sure it''s set on midtones and then desturate...(I think ) blue You''ll get a Yellowish cast. apply your gradient layer. you''ll be surprised at the results', '2003-11-04 13:23:09.000000', NULL, 1),
