(473320, 44999, 13624, '<td valign="top">I like this image a lot. The ripples on the sand, the sand gathering on the clock face and the yellow/blue colouring. Very nice. 9.</td>', 'I like this image a lot. The ripples on the sand, the sand gathering on the clock face and the yellow/blue colouring. Very nice. 9.', '2003-11-05 08:41:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(473325, 45125, 13624, '<td valign="top">I like the gritty feel of an industrial subject. The pattern of the track is good. I also like the combination of angle and bottom heavy composition. Very good, 8.</td>', 'I like the gritty feel of an industrial subject. The pattern of the track is good. I also like the combination of angle and bottom heavy composition. Very good, 8.', '2003-11-05 08:45:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(473427, 45071, 12661, '<td valign="top">I love the long cloud below the cirrus and the colors from the sun are well captured. Overall, however, I think the photo is a bit dark and grainy.</td>', 'I love the long cloud below the cirrus and the colors from the sun are well captured. Overall, however, I think the photo is a bit dark and grainy.', '2003-11-05 09:52:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(473436, 45073, 12661, '<td valign="top">The subject, color balance, and perspective all work very well in this photo. The only downside is the perpendicular sun lines on the road. It tends to break up the line to infinity. A section of road that was lined up with the sun would have worked better.</td>', 'The subject, color balance, and perspective all work very well in this photo. The only downside is the perpendicular sun lines on the road. It tends to break up the line to infinity. A section of road that was lined up with the sun would have worked better.', '2003-11-05 09:55:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(473444, 45143, 12661, '<td valign="top">I really like the way you aligned the photo along the end of the railroad ties instead of the typicall shot down the middle of the tracks. I think, however, that you cropped a bit too much off the top. I think showing some more sky could have improved the overall image. (I''d have to see it to know for sure though)</td>', 'I really like the way you aligned the photo along the end of the railroad ties instead of the typicall shot down the middle of the tracks. I think, however, that you cropped a bit too much off the top. I think showing some more sky could have improved the overall image. (I''d have to see it to know for sure though)', '2003-11-05 09:58:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(473462, 45101, 12569, '<td valign="top">great skies</td>', 'great skies', '2003-11-05 10:12:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(473463, 45009, 12569, '<td valign="top">it gives me goos-pimples, great!</td>', 'it gives me goos-pimples, great!', '2003-11-05 10:14:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(473464, 45096, 12569, '<td valign="top">wow!</td>', 'wow!', '2003-11-05 10:15:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(473510, 45101, 12661, '<td valign="top">Excellent use of light and nice job capturing the seagull. The only negative is that I think the border is too wide, but everything else makes that insignificant. Very nicely done.</td>', 'Excellent use of light and nice job capturing the seagull. The only negative is that I think the border is too wide, but everything else makes that insignificant. Very nicely done.', '2003-11-05 10:44:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(473955, 45115, 12661, '<td valign="top">Very nice interpretation of the challenge and excellent colors in the photo. I especially like the use of yellow for the inside border. Your composition is either well though out or very lucky. Particularly the placememnt of the minute hand perfectly centered on the 4 o''clock mark and the vertical seconds hand. The only criticism is that the hour hand should have been more distinctly seperated from the minute hand (maybe at the 8:00 position for symetry). Also the scratch on the bezel by the 40 on the top dial is unfortunate. (not just for the photo but for your watch too).  Aside from that, very nicely composed. I like it.</td>', 'Very nice interpretation of the challenge and excellent colors in the photo. I especially like the use of yellow for the inside border. Your composition is either well though out or very lucky. Particularly the placememnt of the minute hand perfectly centered on the 4 o''clock mark and the vertical seconds hand. The only criticism is that the hour hand should have been more distinctly seperated from the minute hand (maybe at the 8:00 position for symetry). Also the scratch on the bezel by the 40 on the top dial is unfortunate. (not just for the photo but for your watch too).  Aside from that, very nicely composed. I like it.', '2003-11-05 14:04:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(473959, 45087, 12661, '<td valign="top">I really like the way the light is caught on the face of each step and the way it converges out at the top right. A very nice looking and pleasing photograph that captures the challenge well. The only thing I don''t like is the title since there are many weeds visible. But this is a photo challenge not a title challenge, so no harm done.</td>', 'I really like the way the light is caught on the face of each step and the way it converges out at the top right. A very nice looking and pleasing photograph that captures the challenge well. The only thing I don''t like is the title since there are many weeds visible. But this is a photo challenge not a title challenge, so no harm done.', '2003-11-05 14:07:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(473977, 44967, 12661, '<td valign="top">Nice interpretation of the challenge. Our lives are finite, but our genes live on through the next generations. I am also impressed by the location of the shot and using the pattern in the fence to emulate the double-helix of DNA. Very well composed.</td>', 'Nice interpretation of the challenge. Our lives are finite, but our genes live on through the next generations. I am also impressed by the location of the shot and using the pattern in the fence to emulate the double-helix of DNA. Very well composed.', '2003-11-05 14:18:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(473981, 45157, 12661, '<td valign="top">The out-of-focuse line at the bottom takes a lot away from the photo as it tends to draw my attention to it. Aside from that, it is very nicely composed and gives an almost serene feeling to the viewer.</td>', 'The out-of-focuse line at the bottom takes a lot away from the photo as it tends to draw my attention to it. Aside from that, it is very nicely composed and gives an almost serene feeling to the viewer.', '2003-11-05 14:19:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(474028, 44961, 12661, '<td valign="top">What a charmin photograph (sorry, couldn''t resist). As far as the photo is concerned, the colors appear too muted. More light could have added a more vibrant contrast. Also, although the title suits the challenge, I have a hard time matching it to the photo and also matching the photo to the challenge. Maybe if you included mom with a stern disciplinary look about her it would have helped bring it all together.</td>', 'What a charmin photograph (sorry, couldn''t resist). As far as the photo is concerned, the colors appear too muted. More light could have added a more vibrant contrast. Also, although the title suits the challenge, I have a hard time matching it to the photo and also matching the photo to the challenge. Maybe if you included mom with a stern disciplinary look about her it would have helped bring it all together.', '2003-11-05 14:50:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(474036, 45049, 7190, '<td valign="top">Really would have been a nice shot you had the theme ,the colors, the texture but too bad the first stalks weren''t in focus and then blend down to the soft fading effect</td>', 'Really would have been a nice shot you had the theme ,the colors, the texture but too bad the first stalks weren''t in focus and then blend down to the soft fading effect', '2003-11-05 14:54:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(474102, 45106, 12661, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the lesson in Osage Oranges. You learn something new everyday.</td>', 'Thanks for the lesson in Osage Oranges. You learn something new everyday.', '2003-11-05 15:46:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(474400, 45009, 7628, '<td valign="top">Marvelous - the lines of the boardwalk curving out to the horizon, those three people toward the end giving us some scale, very nice range of grays.  I might crop a bit off the sky...but perhaps that lends to the feeling of infinite. 9</td>', 'Marvelous - the lines of the boardwalk curving out to the horizon, those three people toward the end giving us some scale, very nice range of grays.  I might crop a bit off the sky...but perhaps that lends to the feeling of infinite. 9', '2003-11-05 18:19:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(474416, 45128, 7628, '<td valign="top">This must have been a lot of work - you got the tea-lights lined up so perfectly.  Nice to have the exposure so that the background is black.  I wish the line of lights came from a corner rather than falling off the top of the picture.  The resolution (?) makes the image a bit grainy.</td>', 'This must have been a lot of work - you got the tea-lights lined up so perfectly.  Nice to have the exposure so that the background is black.  I wish the line of lights came from a corner rather than falling off the top of the picture.  The resolution (?) makes the image a bit grainy.', '2003-11-05 18:29:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(474424, 45156, 7628, '<td valign="top">What lush greens - I like tha balance between the trees and the grass with the section of shadowy trunk and old pine needles between them, a simple, nice composition.  You get the feeling of the age/timelessness of trees. 8</td>', 'What lush greens - I like tha balance between the trees and the grass with the section of shadowy trunk and old pine needles between them, a simple, nice composition.  You get the feeling of the age/timelessness of trees. 8', '2003-11-05 18:35:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(474433, 45087, 7628, '<td valign="top">the curving of the steps really adds to the feeling of the steps stretching on and on.  I like the composition of the steps going up (or down) corner to corner.  Simple lines of light and shadow really with the deatail of the weeds - very nice.</td>', 'the curving of the steps really adds to the feeling of the steps stretching on and on.  I like the composition of the steps going up (or down) corner to corner.  Simple lines of light and shadow really with the deatail of the weeds - very nice.', '2003-11-05 18:41:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(474449, 44578, 7628, '<td valign="top">Lovely corn - it does have almost infinite details and colors.  Perhaps gentler lighting would bring out the richness better without the glare.  Sometime bouncing a light off white paper or a board works nicely, a couple of lights from different angles creates nice shading and gives dimension.  I like the DOF - having the other ear in the background, but out of focus, adds to the infinite effect.</td>', 'Lovely corn - it does have almost infinite details and colors.  Perhaps gentler lighting would bring out the richness better without the glare.  Sometime bouncing a light off white paper or a board works nicely, a couple of lights from different angles creates nice shading and gives dimension.  I like the DOF - having the other ear in the background, but out of focus, adds to the infinite effect.', '2003-11-05 18:47:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(474454, 44832, 13381, '<td valign="top">The refraction of light through the marble gives the image the illusion of floating.  Very cool.  Great use of light and color, and nice shot.</td>', 'The refraction of light through the marble gives the image the illusion of floating.  Very cool.  Great use of light and color, and nice shot.', '2003-11-05 18:49:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(474455, 45143, 7628, '<td valign="top">A classic idea - train tracks to the vanishing point.  More even lighting would be better - the flash just highlights the uninteresting foreground, and takes our attention away from the infinite aspect of the shot.  Crop at the top to get rid of the white building that doesn;t add the to pic.</td>', 'A classic idea - train tracks to the vanishing point.  More even lighting would be better - the flash just highlights the uninteresting foreground, and takes our attention away from the infinite aspect of the shot.  Crop at the top to get rid of the white building that doesn;t add the to pic.', '2003-11-05 18:50:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(474457, 45010, 5792, '<td valign="top">I really like the way rail runs along the edge of the frame. That is a unique perspective. If you had rotated the image a half degree or so it would have been perfectly on the edge. Well done.</td>', 'I really like the way rail runs along the edge of the frame. That is a unique perspective. If you had rotated the image a half degree or so it would have been perfectly on the edge. Well done.', '2003-11-05 18:52:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(474467, 45125, 7628, '<td valign="top">Interesting grainy effect - takes our minds of the details (which could be distracting) and onto the whole of the photo - the abstract infinite.  Wish the vanishing point came exactly in the corner - it is offset to the right.</td>', 'Interesting grainy effect - takes our minds of the details (which could be distracting) and onto the whole of the photo - the abstract infinite.  Wish the vanishing point came exactly in the corner - it is offset to the right.', '2003-11-05 18:54:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(474470, 44537, 5792, '<td valign="top">I look forward to reading photographer comments on this one. Looks like it might have been taken inside a planatarium.</td>', 'I look forward to reading photographer comments on this one. Looks like it might have been taken inside a planatarium.', '2003-11-05 18:55:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(474482, 45104, 7628, '<td valign="top">Wow!  The range of textures - the shiny ice, the spikey grass, the choppy waves, the misty hills, the range of white to black.  Nicely balances composition with the rails coming down from the curve of the shore to the rock and ice along the bottom, the lonely hut peering out of the dark bushes.  I wish the left most edge of the rail wasn''t cut off...but that is a little thing.  Is this Iceland?  This is something I''d hang on the wall! 10</td>', 'Wow!  The range of textures - the shiny ice, the spikey grass, the choppy waves, the misty hills, the range of white to black.  Nicely balances composition with the rails coming down from the curve of the shore to the rock and ice along the bottom, the lonely hut peering out of the dark bushes.  I wish the left most edge of the rail wasn''t cut off...but that is a little thing.  Is this Iceland?  This is something I''d hang on the wall! 10', '2003-11-05 18:59:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(474506, 44522, 5792, '<td valign="top">This spectacular image, I''d guess, would score more than a half point higher in voting if touched up with NeatImage... You can see my temporary adjustment to it at.. //www.pbase.com/image/23025194 <br/> <br/>I will delete it after you have had a chance to see it. Great picture.</td>', 'This spectacular image, I''d guess, would score more than a half point higher in voting if touched up with NeatImage... You can see my temporary adjustment to it at.. //www.pbase.com/image/23025194  I will delete it after you have had a chance to see it. Great picture.', '2003-11-05 19:12:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(474518, 45134, 11487, '<td valign="top">Nice perspective and composition.  Meets the challenge well.  B&amp;W works well for this image, not sure color would work as well-good choice.</td>', 'Nice perspective and composition.  Meets the challenge well.  B&W works well for this image, not sure color would work as well-good choice.', '2003-11-05 19:16:10.000000', NULL, 1),
