(477561, 44888, 1031, '<td valign="top">I considered doing something like this with a Moebius strip.</td>', 'I considered doing something like this with a Moebius strip.', '2003-11-08 18:41:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(477577, 44484, 1031, '<td valign="top">I think this came out better than the one I was thinking of doing!</td>', 'I think this came out better than the one I was thinking of doing!', '2003-11-08 18:56:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(477582, 44935, 11923, '<td valign="top">Heh, cute title.  I like the image, the angles shown are great, works very well in black &amp; white.  Has a nice added crispness.  Lighting is good, composition is too.  I like that the subject isn''t looking directly into the camera, gives her an impish look.  Really the only thing I''d change is minor - would rather the focus was sharper across the bottom so everything was in focus, but its only a tiny thing.  Very well done.  9</td>', 'Heh, cute title.  I like the image, the angles shown are great, works very well in black & white.  Has a nice added crispness.  Lighting is good, composition is too.  I like that the subject isn''t looking directly into the camera, gives her an impish look.  Really the only thing I''d change is minor - would rather the focus was sharper across the bottom so everything was in focus, but its only a tiny thing.  Very well done.  9', '2003-11-08 19:02:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(477585, 44629, 1031, '<td valign="top">Interesting that I just heard this week that Voyager I has (or is about to) crossed the point demarcating the Sun''s sphere of influence, marking humankind''s first official incursion into interstellar space. So good of you to take the time to travel out there and document it for us.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-11-12 19:47:15.</i></td>', 'Interesting that I just heard this week that Voyager I has (or is about to) crossed the point demarcating the Sun''s sphere of influence, marking humankind''s first official incursion into interstellar space. So good of you to take the time to travel out there and document it for us.', '2003-11-08 19:06:22.000000', '2003-11-12 19:47:15.000000', 1),
(477586, 45088, 11923, '<td valign="top">Fits the challenge, the lighting is good, though a bit harsh on the horizon.  Nice contrasts in colors.  I wish the focus was a little sharper and there weren''t those streaks across the sky (powerlines?).  Also the image looks slightly tilted, which could be a nice interest point if it was more exaggerated - but as is, I find it more distracting than not.  Its a good shot, just needs some tightening up.  5</td>', 'Fits the challenge, the lighting is good, though a bit harsh on the horizon.  Nice contrasts in colors.  I wish the focus was a little sharper and there weren''t those streaks across the sky (powerlines?).  Also the image looks slightly tilted, which could be a nice interest point if it was more exaggerated - but as is, I find it more distracting than not.  Its a good shot, just needs some tightening up.  5', '2003-11-08 19:07:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(477587, 45169, 1031, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure your combination of mathematical props works -- Pi is endless and non-repeating and the strip is endlessly repeating. You did a pretty gog job with the photo though!</td>', 'I''m not sure your combination of mathematical props works -- Pi is endless and non-repeating and the strip is endlessly repeating. You did a pretty gog job with the photo though!', '2003-11-08 19:08:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(477588, 44582, 11923, '<td valign="top">Great composition.  Everything looks in place, I don''t know math (ugh) so I don''t know how accurate the equations are but they look the part.  Nice range of items around, good lighting, the focus is good but I do wish it was a little bit crisper, not sure if that''s due to resizing or not.  I really like the thought and effort that went into the details of this - the one thing that really does it for me is that ring from the coffee on the paper.  Excellent.   9</td>', 'Great composition.  Everything looks in place, I don''t know math (ugh) so I don''t know how accurate the equations are but they look the part.  Nice range of items around, good lighting, the focus is good but I do wish it was a little bit crisper, not sure if that''s due to resizing or not.  I really like the thought and effort that went into the details of this - the one thing that really does it for me is that ring from the coffee on the paper.  Excellent.   9', '2003-11-08 19:10:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(477589, 44899, 1031, '<td valign="top">Good idea ... I have some stuff like that but didn''t think to use it for this.</td>', 'Good idea ... I have some stuff like that but didn''t think to use it for this.', '2003-11-08 19:12:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(477590, 45006, 1031, '<td valign="top">You did a lot with a little!</td>', 'You did a lot with a little!', '2003-11-08 19:13:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(477591, 45104, 11923, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous photo.  I love the way ice looks in black &amp; white.  This has a very haunting look, the play between the moving water and the frozen water is great.  That little house nestled in adds even more interest.  Simply beautiful.  That said, I find the connection to infinite tenuous based only on the photo (doesn''t say infinite to me) - its mostly inferred by the title - but I *can* see the possibility of an never-ending winter occurring somewhere in the frigid north.  Very lovely shot.   8</td>', 'Gorgeous photo.  I love the way ice looks in black & white.  This has a very haunting look, the play between the moving water and the frozen water is great.  That little house nestled in adds even more interest.  Simply beautiful.  That said, I find the connection to infinite tenuous based only on the photo (doesn''t say infinite to me) - its mostly inferred by the title - but I *can* see the possibility of an never-ending winter occurring somewhere in the frigid north.  Very lovely shot.   8', '2003-11-08 19:13:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(477648, 45101, 8816, '<td valign="top">Very cool photo.  Love the whole feeling of the shot, the dark forboding (ya I can''t spell) sky is accented so well by the evil feeling of the silhouetted building, and the solitary bid.  Very nice!  I don''t see how this fits inifinity, but I give it a 9 none the less.</td>', 'Very cool photo.  Love the whole feeling of the shot, the dark forboding (ya I can''t spell) sky is accented so well by the evil feeling of the silhouetted building, and the solitary bid.  Very nice!  I don''t see how this fits inifinity, but I give it a 9 none the less.', '2003-11-08 20:49:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(477670, 44899, 13440, '<td valign="top">I like the pattern of the subject... What''s it?</td>', 'I like the pattern of the subject... What''s it?', '2003-11-08 21:22:16.000000', NULL, 1),
