(478386, 44981, 3295, '<td valign="top">What the hell is wrong with people... A 1 someone voted!!!  Yikes... Great Pic.</td>', 'What the hell is wrong with people... A 1 someone voted!!!  Yikes... Great Pic.', '2003-11-10 00:02:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(478387, 45115, 11855, '<td valign="top">thanks for the comments... spinning hands and more seperation would have improved it. Great input!</td>', 'thanks for the comments... spinning hands and more seperation would have improved it. Great input!', '2003-11-10 00:03:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(478388, 44999, 806, '<td valign="top">outstanding image! congrats!</td>', 'outstanding image! congrats!', '2003-11-10 00:04:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(478389, 44999, 10170, '<td valign="top">This was my pick for a win, though the 1st and 2nd place are excellent.  REALLY glad this got a ribbon though.<br/> <br/>Congrats :)</td>', 'This was my pick for a win, though the 1st and 2nd place are excellent.  REALLY glad this got a ribbon though. Congrats :)', '2003-11-10 00:06:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(478397, 44999, 9146, '<td valign="top">congrats this shot is awsome</td>', 'congrats this shot is awsome', '2003-11-10 00:15:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(478399, 44981, 255, '<td valign="top">congrats andre! gorgeous pic--my fav of the challenge! :)</td>', 'congrats andre! gorgeous pic--my fav of the challenge! :)', '2003-11-10 00:18:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(478405, 44981, 7687, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot, congratulations!</td>', 'Beautiful shot, congratulations!', '2003-11-10 00:22:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(478408, 44904, 12253, '<td valign="top">This is an awesome shot.  I felt it stated infinity better than all of the others combined.  You were my bet to win, next to mine ;-)</td>', 'This is an awesome shot.  I felt it stated infinity better than all of the others combined.  You were my bet to win, next to mine ;-)', '2003-11-10 00:27:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(478410, 45012, 11800, '<td valign="top">Sorry you didn''t win. I still think this is one of the most beautiful pictures on this site. How did you set it up? If you don''t mind sharing.<br/>Is it ice?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-11-10 02:47:33.</i></td>', 'Sorry you didn''t win. I still think this is one of the most beautiful pictures on this site. How did you set it up? If you don''t mind sharing.Is it ice?', '2003-11-10 00:27:45.000000', '2003-11-10 02:47:33.000000', 0),
(478412, 44999, 6804, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! I was glad to see this shot win.</td>', 'Congratulations! I was glad to see this shot win.', '2003-11-10 00:29:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(478420, 44981, 6804, '<td valign="top">Awesome shot Refracted, Ive never seen the Aurora Borealis as vivid as you have managed to capture with this shot.  Congratulations on the win.</td>', 'Awesome shot Refracted, Ive never seen the Aurora Borealis as vivid as you have managed to capture with this shot.  Congratulations on the win.', '2003-11-10 00:31:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(478422, 44935, 11800, '<td valign="top">Great shot Deannda. I''m glad it did so well for you. It was one of my favorites.</td>', 'Great shot Deannda. I''m glad it did so well for you. It was one of my favorites.', '2003-11-10 00:32:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(478427, 44999, 7687, '<td valign="top">My first ribbon, what a great feeling, thanks everyone for the votes and the great comments.<br/> <br/>The way I achieved the ripples in the sand was by first smoothing it all out, then dragging my fingers through it.  I stuck the clocks in the sand, grabbed a handful of sand which I poured over the clocks and threw some lightly at the ripples to knock down the peaks.  I followed that by touching up the ripples with my fingers.  After than I blew on the face of the bottom clock to give the sand a a "windblown" look.<br/> <br/></td>', 'My first ribbon, what a great feeling, thanks everyone for the votes and the great comments. The way I achieved the ripples in the sand was by first smoothing it all out, then dragging my fingers through it.  I stuck the clocks in the sand, grabbed a handful of sand which I poured over the clocks and threw some lightly at the ripples to knock down the peaks.  I followed that by touching up the ripples with my fingers.  After than I blew on the face of the bottom clock to give the sand a a "windblown" look. ', '2003-11-10 00:33:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(478441, 44999, 13440, '<td valign="top">I think your Photograph Information was wrong...<br/>Congratulation! I gave you 10!</td>', 'I think your Photograph Information was wrong...Congratulation! I gave you 10!', '2003-11-10 00:46:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(478448, 44619, 6035, '<td valign="top">Great shot Gringo, and congrats on the finish.. gave this a 10 myself and was worried a bit about it :) it was a close one.</td>', 'Great shot Gringo, and congrats on the finish.. gave this a 10 myself and was worried a bit about it :) it was a close one.', '2003-11-10 00:56:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(478452, 44935, 8953, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your very strong showing...I remember well when I started working my way through the ranks. I know as hard as you work to be a part of this community, you deserved at least this spot. Good luck to future challenges!<br/> <br/>Richard</td>', 'Congrats on your very strong showing...I remember well when I started working my way through the ranks. I know as hard as you work to be a part of this community, you deserved at least this spot. Good luck to future challenges! Richard', '2003-11-10 00:58:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(478453, 44981, 6035, '<td valign="top">thanks everyone :) it was an amazing night of auroras, and for those who might be wondering, i did no hue adjustments. Only some slight leveling (to actually tone down the colors) and crop/resize.</td>', 'thanks everyone :) it was an amazing night of auroras, and for those who might be wondering, i did no hue adjustments. Only some slight leveling (to actually tone down the colors) and crop/resize.', '2003-11-10 00:58:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(478458, 44947, 2667, '<td valign="top">Great shot, Pat. We must have been battling for position until the final tally! <br/> <br/>What I find most interesting, though, is that we both entered wavy, rippling abstract pieces to depict infinity... something very few others attempted. Maybe it has something to do with the chemicals released when using the SD9. Does yours give you a buzz?<br/> <br/>Congrats on the great finish, <br/> <br/>Michael<br/> <br/></td>', 'Great shot, Pat. We must have been battling for position until the final tally!  What I find most interesting, though, is that we both entered wavy, rippling abstract pieces to depict infinity... something very few others attempted. Maybe it has something to do with the chemicals released when using the SD9. Does yours give you a buzz? Congrats on the great finish,  Michael ', '2003-11-10 01:05:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(478461, 44935, 11078, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a great shot and I know how excited you must feel to have a good ranking Well done!<br/>I have done one of my best this time and I am thrilled. although I did like my water lily and have that framed on my dinning room wall I keep showing my family all the time I think they are sick of me Ha ha <br/>I am aiming to get on the first page soon<br/>I like to know who these people are that rate 1''s  I have a few as well<br/>They must do it to everyone. and totally unfair.<br/>Sally<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-11-10 01:11:16.</i></td>', 'I thought this was a great shot and I know how excited you must feel to have a good ranking Well done!I have done one of my best this time and I am thrilled. although I did like my water lily and have that framed on my dinning room wall I keep showing my family all the time I think they are sick of me Ha ha I am aiming to get on the first page soonI like to know who these people are that rate 1''s  I have a few as wellThey must do it to everyone. and totally unfair.Sally', '2003-11-10 01:07:38.000000', '2003-11-10 01:11:16.000000', 0),
